# Models — Anêmicos

Models Eloquent com responsabilidade única: estrutura, relacionamentos, scopes e casts. Nada mais.

## Estrutura Obrigatória

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Models;

use App\Casts\MoneyCast;
use App\Enums\OrderStatus;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Factories\HasFactory;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Relations\BelongsTo;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Relations\HasMany;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\SoftDeletes;

final class Order extends Model
{
    use HasFactory;
    use SoftDeletes;

    protected $fillable = [
        'customer_id',
        'status',
        'payment_method',
        'total',
    ];

    protected $casts = [
        'status' => OrderStatus::class,
        'total'  => MoneyCast::class,
    ];

    // Relacionamentos
    public function customer(): BelongsTo
    {
        return $this->belongsTo(Customer::class);
    }

    public function items(): HasMany
    {
        return $this->hasMany(OrderItem::class);
    }

    // Scopes
    public function scopePending($query): mixed
    {
        return $query->where('status', OrderStatus::Pending);
    }

    // Helpers de estado (sem lógica de negócio)
    public function isFinalized(): bool
    {
        return $this->status->isFinalized();
    }

    public function hasPayment(): bool
    {
        return $this->payment !== null;
    }
}
```

## Custom Casts — Integração com Value Objects

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Casts;

use App\ValueObjects\Money;
use Illuminate\Contracts\Database\Eloquent\CastsAttributes;
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Model;

final class MoneyCast implements CastsAttributes
{
    public function get(Model $model, string $key, mixed $value, array $attributes): Money
    {
        return Money::fromCents((int) $value);
    }

    public function set(Model $model, string $key, mixed $value, array $attributes): int
    {
        return $value instanceof Money
            ? $value->toCents()
            : (int) $value;
    }
}
```

## Enums

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

namespace App\Enums;

enum OrderStatus: string
{
    case Pending   = 'pending';
    case Confirmed = 'confirmed';
    case Shipped   = 'shipped';
    case Delivered = 'delivered';
    case Cancelled = 'cancelled';

    public function label(): string
    {
        return match($this) {
            self::Pending   => 'Aguardando',
            self::Confirmed => 'Confirmado',
            self::Shipped   => 'Enviado',
            self::Delivered => 'Entregue',
            self::Cancelled => 'Cancelado',
        };
    }

    public function isFinalized(): bool
    {
        return in_array($this, [self::Delivered, self::Cancelled], true);
    }
}
```

## Regras

- Classe `final` — sem herança de models
- Use `$fillable` **ou** `$guarded` — nunca os dois
- Use `$casts` para enums, datas, booleans, JSON e Value Objects
- Nunca coloque regras de negócio, queries complexas ou chamadas externas em models
- Observers separados em `app/Observers/` para eventos de model
- Sem lógica nos mutators — use Value Objects com Custom Casts
- Helpers de estado (`isFinalized()`, `hasPayment()`) são permitidos — delegam para o Enum ou checam atributo simples
- Organize Casts em `app/Casts/` e Enums em `app/Enums/`

## Anti-Patterns

```php
// ❌ Lógica de negócio no model
class Order extends Model {
    public function finalize(): void {
        Mail::send(...); // nunca — use Event + Listener
        $this->status = 'finalized';
        $this->save();
    }
}

// ❌ Herança de models
class PremiumOrder extends Order {} // nunca — use scopes ou polimorfismo

// ❌ Constantes no lugar de Enum
class Order extends Model {
    const STATUS_PENDING = 'pending'; // use enum OrderStatus
}

// ❌ Query complexa no model
class Order extends Model {
    public static function getPendingWithExpiredItems(): Collection {
        return self::where(...)->join(...)->get(); // mova para Repository ou Service
    }
}

// ❌ $fillable e $guarded juntos
protected $fillable = [...];
protected $guarded = []; // escolha um
```
